# Exclusions for backend/Dockerfile only.
#
# Named `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`, which BuildKit reads in preference to a
# context-root `.dockerignore`. That is the point: this build takes the REPOSITORY
# ROOT as its context, and a root-level `.dockerignore` would be a repository-wide
# file affecting anything else built here. This one cannot reach past this Dockerfile.
#
# The first entry is the one that matters. `.env` holds OPENROUTER_API_KEY in local
# development, `COPY backend/ ./` would otherwise bake it into an image layer, and a
# credential in a layer survives deletion of the file in a later one.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Runtime data: uploads, stored reviews, status files. Can be large, is never part
# of a build, and may contain submitted customer designs.
**/local-data/

# Test suite, fixtures and the standalone scripts. None is imported by the running
# app — main.py -> api.routes -> agent/ingestion reaches none of them — and the
# ground-truth fixtures carry labelled designs that have no business in a
# production image. Note this means the image cannot run pytest; that is deliberate,
# and CI runs the suite from a checkout rather than from this image.
backend/tests/
backend/scripts/
fixtures/
docs/

# Frontend, tooling and VCS metadata. Nothing under these is read by the backend.
frontend/
scripts/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/node_modules/
*.md
!backend/README.md
